%N A401844 Number of integers k where n^2 < k < (n+1)^2 such that the period of the continued fraction of the square root of k is an even number.
%H A401844 Oleg Smolyakov, <a href="/A401844/b401844.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%F A401844 a(n) = 2*n - A401843(n).
%e A401844 a(7) = 10. For all k (49 < k < 64), according to A003285, only 10 numbers have an even period for the continued fraction of the square root of k; namely: 51, 52, 54, 55, 56, 57, 59, 60, 61, and 63.
